WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.680
My passionate idol activities,

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.470
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.440
So far on Aikatsu!

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:16.460
I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo, a third-year at the idol school Starlight Academy.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.620
We all use Aikatsu cards to do our idol activities.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:25.710
Saegusa Kii-chan from Dream Academy's producer course made her idol debut last time.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.250
I feel like Aikatsu is going to get more passionate now!

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:35.840
Headmistress!

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.410
Hi there, you three.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:39.390
On your way home?

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.410
Yes.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.850
I just got out of a business meeting.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.890
Want to go back together?

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.110
Sure!

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:51.530
Kiriya, <i>Naughty Police Chief</i> was a big hit.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.030
Thank you.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.910
The upcoming TV special looks quite interesting.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.130
Yes, it really is.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.160
What's it about?

00:00:59.160 --> 00:00:59.910
It's this.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.210
"Naughty Police Chief: Could it be first love?" {or itals}

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:03.660
Yep!

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.000
Love, huh?

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.570
Like the thing that climbs up waterfalls?

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.390
You're thinking of koi fish. {should I even try}

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:11.770
This is romantic love.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:12.760
What Aoi was talking about... {timing}

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.050
<i>I wonder who that is.</i>

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.160
Kii-chan, this is going to be your first real gig, right?

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:20.930
Yes.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.600
This time I'll pro-pro-produce myself properly! {ugh, it's like two lines from the ED spliced together}

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:28.480
Of course, I'll keep being Seira's producer too.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.230
Forget about that. Just focus on yourself for now.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.090
<i>No doubt about it. That's Mister S.</i>

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:40.240
<i>He's a reporter famous for exposing idols' love affairs.</i>

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.230
Headmistress Tiara?

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:43.820
It's nothing.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.620
Let's go!

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.000
<i>Who is he going after this time? {whom, technically}</i>

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:27.720
This is bad!

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.190
I found out who that mysterious man was!

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.440
Huh, him...

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.330
I saw him at the TV station.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.950
His name is Mister S.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:40.400
Who?

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.050
He's a famous reporter in the business.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.830
They say he always gets the dirt he wants.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.950
He's exposed countless celebrities' secrets. {spell check is telling me the ' is wrong}

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.710
There was a scandal with an actress and her lover just a while back.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.340
Mister S was the one who dug that up.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.600
Yeah.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.190
The scandals are mostly about people's love lives

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:03.220
and other things you wouldn't want others to know.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.670
The S in Mister S stands for "secret".

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.030
For "scoop".

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.220
For "scandal"!

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.190
So what was Mister S doing at the TV station?

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.100
He definitely got wind of a scandal...

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.680
...and was looking into it.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.170
Mister S was probably trying to expose some sort of scandal with you, Seira.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.570
In case you didn't know,

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.180
scandals are like that time when Starlight's Toudou Yurika's true self was revealed.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.240
You mean the vampire character, Yurika-sama?

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:30.310
Yes.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.450
It turned out that the self-assured 
Yurika-sama was actually <i>this</i> cute, {a million words for tsuyoki and I can't think of one that fits}

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:38.550
and that she actually loved garlic, which vampires are supposed to hate.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.130
It was a big scandal,

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:45.010
but the gap between her character and her true self was really attractive, so she gained a lot of fans.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.090
Wow.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.200
Yeah.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.520
So with you, it'd be about how you used to be in a rock band with your friends,

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.330
or about how you used to play classical music before that,

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.900
or about how you have absolute pitch.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.580
None of that is secret.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.770
That cat's already out of the bag. {I love doing this}

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:03.670
If Mister S is going after something other than what I just said,

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.660
he must be going after your lovey-cutesy side! {dddasgnitrom}{just ridiculous enough to work}

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.650
What? That?

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:09.930
That's not really a secret either—

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:10.990
No!

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.070
From here on out, don't say a single word about that.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.750
Is it really that big a deal?

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.030
It is!

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.330
As your producer I have to say,

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.630
no way, no way, no way!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.490
Kii, didn't you just get your own job?

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.130
Shouldn't you be getting ready for that?

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.760
As long as I have the Aikatsu drink, Brain Thunder, I'll be ok-ok-okay!

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.780
<i>Will we really be okay like this?</i>

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.780
Good morning, Kiriya-honey!

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:52.370
Despite what you may think, I prefer my eggs sunny-side up with soy sauce! {I am confused}{maybe that's his scandal?}

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.080
I like mine with just some salt and pepper.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.500
I know it's short notice, Kiriya,

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:59.230
but there's a job I want you to take.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:05:59.790
Okay.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.420
Ah, Aikatsu Navi.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.580
Correct.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.370
The magazine <i>Aikatsu Navi</i> just announced that they will be sponsoring a fashion show.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.800
They wanted you to participate.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.270
Me?

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:14.060
Yes.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:17.440
This fashion show has a theme.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.060
And that theme is most decidedly...

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.820
First love!

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:21.690
Hatsukoi. {iguntronowenovtriboerogfhiiwerogfjierojg; also, why does no one else have a short name for 初めての恋が終わる時, it's too long and clause-y to say fully (in both Japanese and English)}{I say leave it... yeah, leave it}

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.070
First love?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.200
Yes.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:30.870
They asked if Kiriya Aoi-san, the star of <i>Naughty Police Chief: The Feeling of First Love</i>, could participate. {note, I added the -san}

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.950
They're going after the whole "first love" thing.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.240
Oh.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.710
DreAca's Kii-chan-honey is also going to appear. {I know standard policy is to squish all honorifics together, but I don't think that works with honorifics that are English words}{sure}

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.830
They said that since she just made her idol debut,

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:44.590
she fit the theme of "first love" perfectly.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.050
Really?

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.340
Is something the matter?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:51.070
I don't have much experience with modeling,

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.970
but I'll make you proud.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.430
Good. I know you can do it. {not sure if that was intentional or not}

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.290
Good luck, Kiriya-honey.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.010
Thanks.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:00.600
Um, Headmistress...

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.590
What is it?

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.630
This is about Mister S.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:05.860
I saw him at the TV station.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:07.610
So you noticed too?

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:12.010
It's definitely true that Mister S is digging up some sort of scandal.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:13.240
Just be careful.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.740
Okay.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.750
Ai-katsu. Ai-katsu.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:21.000
Ai-katsu. Ai-katsu.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:24.500
Imagine that there's a thread 
holding your head straight up. {or chin}

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.130
Yes!

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.230
Thanks for coming along with me.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:34.710
Of course.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.140
Ah, Suzukawa-san.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.760
Hoshimiya, haven't seen you in a while.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.070
Did something happen to you guys?

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.780
Mister S is after us!

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.270
You mean <i>that</i> Mister S?

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.650
Yeah, <i>that</i> Mister S.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.270
I saw him at the TV station.

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.030
Huh.

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:52.530
But still... {why was this missing?}

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.780
No matter how good he is, there's no way he'd make it onto school grounds.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.270
You can never be too safe.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:00.990
We always have to be on guard.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:01.790
Now then!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:07.630
Come to think of it, do they even have any secrets they'd need to hide?

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:23.620
What if Mister S isn't going after Starlight Academy,

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:24.790
but Tiara's...

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:26.980
We're finally back!

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.020
I'm so tired.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.110
But we have to make double sure our secrets don't get out. {I like it}

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.870
Like how Ichigo performs perfect customer service in her sleep...

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.450
Hey, welcome!

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.370
One seaweed bento coming right up!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:44.840
Or that my perfect collection of <i>Idol Freak Daily</i>

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:48.880
is actually missing the leap year special from February 29th!

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.840
