00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:55.340
I'm supposed to be an idol professor! It has to be top secret!

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:56.640
I didn't know.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.010
And you, Ran!

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:03.210
All your favorite snacks are incredibly plain.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.600
They're like, way too plain!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.280
I-Isn't that fine?

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.460
Why would that turn into a scandal?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:12.070
Aren't scandals usually about love and affairs and stuff?

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.570
For idols, love is a serious matter. {serious business}{I wish it fit}

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:15.860
It is.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.190
I still want to have a wonderful relationship someday. {this is the second "proper" you've inserted}

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:21.290
Like my mom and dad.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:25.740
Love, huh.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:26.500
Yeah.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.030
Good morning!

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:38.140
Today, I'll keep on pro-pro-producing both Seira and myself!

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.480
Mister S...

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.650
He's here to uncover a scandal!

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:15.300
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.610
Seira-chan! Kii-chan!

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:18.430
What's up?

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:20.430
Give us asylum! {to use a big word, but it doesn't fit thaat well}{it's fine, but I'm pretty sure later on they use some sort of word or something... (later) nevermind, it's cool}

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.830
Kii-chan, are you okay?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:26.430
Yeah.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:29.480
I'm surprised DreAca students keep getting in so easily.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:31.810
We asked the groundskeeper guy. {why does aegisub say groundskeeper is not a word, but groundskeepers is}{Don't think you actually need "guy" here}

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:33.820
Suzukawa-san!

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.740
Yeah.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:38.200
But something major must have happened for you to be seeking asylum.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.790
Seeking asylum means there's someone you're running from.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.700
So there's someone chasing you?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.950
Yes. Mister S.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:46.950
Mister S?

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.830
Don't tell me he already revealed our secrets! {the other ja}

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.080
No, no!

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:54.130
How Ichigo serves guests perfectly in her sleep, {sounds lewd}{less lewd, also not really necessary, so change back if you want}

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:57.530
how Aoi-chan's collection of <i>Idol Freak Daily</i>

00:10:57.530 --> 00:11:01.090
is missing the leap year special from February 29th,

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:05.100
and how the Beautiful Blade Ran-chan's favorite snacks are all really plain foods

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.850
is not what I'm talking about!

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:07.870
Wow.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.130
She has all our secrets.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:11.350
Why do you know all that?

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.480
Trade secret.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:18.030
Isn't it awesome how my sister sells bento in her sleep?

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.240
Amazing! That's so Ichigo-chan!

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.870
Is this article about Aoi-chan true too?

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:26.370
It is! It bugs her so much that she doesn't have that one issue!

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.090
I really want to know who told you.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.910
If Mister S isn't after our information,

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:36.000
